  "generated_text": ".. Calculate the expression inside the square root:\n   \\[\n   (31)(30)(29)(28) + 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   31 \\times 30 = 930\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 29 = 26970\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   26970 \\times 28 = 767160\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   767160 + 1 = 767161\n   \\]\n\n2. Find the square root of 767161:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{767161 = = 877\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\(\\boxed{877}\\)",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[877, '877']",
    "gold_answer": "Let $x = 29.$ Then we can write \\[\\begin{aligned} (31)(30)(29)(28) + 1 &= (x+2)(x+1)(x)(x-1) + 1 \\\\ &= [(x+2)(x-1)][(x+1)x] - 1 \\\\& = (x^2+x-2)(x^2+x) + 1 \\\\&= (x^2+x)^2 - 2(x^2+x) + 1 \\\\&= (x^2+x-1)^2. \\end{aligned} \\]Therefore, the answer is \\[ \\begin{aligned} x^2+x-1&= 29^2 + 29 - 1\\\\& = \\boxed{869}. \\end{aligned}\\]",
    "is_correct": false
  },
